WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.867
Two rival

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.369
rulings on medical abortion

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.637
pills came down yesterday,

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.939
the first from Texas,

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:06.573
a federal judge

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.908
ruling to suspend the FDA's two decade

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.111
old approval of MS. Firestone.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.013
Then just 2 hours later,

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:14.514
a federal judge in Washington

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.115
state ruling

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.416
that FDA must

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.518
keep the medication abortion

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.519
on the shelves.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.521
In 17 Democratic states

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.023
and the District of Columbia.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:23.723
President Biden

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.558
is vowing to fight this ruling.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.794
The DOJ and the FDA have already filed

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.029
separate appeals.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:29.629
Vice President

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.464
Harris told reporters Friday night

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.400
that courts should not be allowed

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.969
to tell the FDA what it can do.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.241
This is a drug that the FDA approved

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.877
as safe might be years ago

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:47.113
and has been proven to be safe

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:49.182
for 20 years.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.251
So this is a dangerous precedent.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.421
Mifepristone is part of the

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.589
most common abortion method in the US.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:58.358
Data from hundreds of studies

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.326
have shown that it is highly safe

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:01.694
and effective.

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.063
Its safety is on par

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:03.797
with common

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.131
over-the-counter pain relievers

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.567
like ibuprofen and acetaminophen.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.101
We're joined now

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.437
by CNN's Elizabeth Cohen.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:13.540
Explain how widely this is used and talk

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.242
more about the safety

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:17.977
Right, Victor.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.779
It's been used very widely

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:20.880
and it is very safe.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.015
I think a lot of people don't know

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:22.882
that actually

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.784
there are more abortions done now

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.686
with the pills than done surgically.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.054
Let's take a look at how

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.489
that's increased over the years.

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.391
So since 20, 20,

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:32.559
it's gone up and up

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.893
and up to the point now

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.296
where more than 53% of abortions

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.097
in the U.S.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.731
are done with pills

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.567
or medication abortions.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.701
And let's take a look

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.169
at some of the side effects.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.105
You know, drugs have side effects

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.107
when we look at deadly side effects

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.908
for every million women

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.743
who have used math for Princeton.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.712
There have been 20 deaths.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.147
If you look at penicillin

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.548
if you look at Viagra

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.283
it's many more for penicillin

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.252
it's 20 deaths per million users.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.221
For Viagra it's 49 deaths

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.355
per million users.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.056
So actually

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.958
when you look at deadly side effects,

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.960
the first stone is safer

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.194
than many other drugs,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.662
not just these two.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.830
Victor and Elizabeth,

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.398
could you talk about

00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:13.166
how this ruling

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:15.401
could have long term impacts

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.738
on the trust in the FDA approval process?

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.841
Yes, there is a lot

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.743
of trust in the FDA approval process.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.845
It has been there for many, many decades.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.780
And other countries besides the U.S.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.048
also rely on it

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.583
because it is a good process.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.784
It is rigorous.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.919
And so drug companies

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.087
apply the

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.555
there's a team of scientists

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:36.990
or teams of scientists

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:37.924
at the FDA

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.626
and outside advisers who weigh in

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.161
on whether or not it should be approved.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.629
And here, one judge

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.664
all by his lonesome has said, now,

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.699
I disagree with all of those experts.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:47.700
I don't think this drug

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.768
should be on the market.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.403
So you can imagine the drug companies

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.138
when they hear this think, wait a second,

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.373
are we going to invest

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.674
millions of dollars

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.709
in drugs, in life saving drugs?

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.845
If a single judge can just say,

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.880
now that needs to come off the market,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.916
that is problematic for drug development

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.951
and that affects all of us.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.552
Sure does.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.619
Elizabeth Cohen,

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.754
appreciate your reporting.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.055
Thank you very much.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.156
Emergency physician

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.357
and deputy dean

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.458
at Brown University

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.993
School of Public Health, Dr.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.329
Megan Ranney, joining us now.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:16.696
Dr.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:16.896
I mean,

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.298
this is the most common

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:19.065
abortion method

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:19.632
in the U.S.,

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.700
as we just heard

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.269
Elizabeth Cohen report there.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:23.703
First off,

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.305
I just want to get your reaction

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:26.072
to this ruling

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.444
I am flabbergasted by this ruling

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.780
for a judge who has no scientific

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.283
training to overturn a panel of experts

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.818
who advise the FDA

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:39.519
on the safety

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.688
and efficacy of a medication

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.890
is frankly unprecedented.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:47.260
Not only was this medication approved

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:49.996
23, almost 23 years ago,

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.598
but it's also undergone

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:54.234
incredibly rigorous safety monitoring

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:54.934
since then.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.502
It is part of a

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.904
special monitoring program

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:01.040
that is applied to only a handful

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:01.774
of medications

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:02.875
across the United States,

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:05.044
recognizing that this is a medication

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.547
that is unfortunately subjected

00:04:07.547 --> 00:04:09.449
to some political debate.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:10.950
And let me be clear,

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.452
as Elizabeth outlined,

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.754
the medication is tremendously safe.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.656
It is actually far safer

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.491
to have a medication abortion

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.460
than to undergo childbirth

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.296
in terms of the likelihood of severe

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.932
effects on the body and hospitalization.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.367
We don't know

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.568
ultimately what will happen

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:29.435
with this ruling

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.336
because as we

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.138
know, appeals are now underway.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:33.106
And this

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.641
ruling that puts a pause

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:36.442
on this particular

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:39.012
medication abortion pill does not take

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:40.913
effect, are not expected to take effect

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.882
until about a week from now.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.084
But in terms of the confusion

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:46.753
that this is going to cause,

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:48.354
let's start from the doctors then

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.188
and the providers.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.556
And I mean,

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.224
I guess

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.259
there might be a scramble now to find

00:04:54.027 --> 00:04:55.328
a different medication

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:58.665
This is certainly

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:01.334
something that has been under discussion

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.769
for months.

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.771
Among those who do provide

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.572
medication, abortions

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.473
for today

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:08.341
in states

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.710
where medication abortion is legal.

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.812
Nothing changes.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:15.515
But we are waiting to see what happens

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.582
next.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.851
At this point, the FDA has said

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.253
this is still a

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.455
safe and efficacious medication.

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:23.523
So for folks

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.891
that are have an appointment,

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:26.759
still show up for your appointment

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:27.694
for doctors

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:28.961
who are planning to prescribe,

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:30.663
they are getting guidance

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.964
from the American College

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:32.598
of Obstetrics

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.900
and Gynecology,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.168
from the American Association

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.536
of Family Physicians

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:38.671
and from other specialty societies

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.073
that help us decide

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:40.473
kind of what

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:41.941
the right next thing to do

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.343
is for our patients

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:44.310
in the context of these

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.545
conflicting legal rulings.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:46.679
We are not lawyers. Right.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:47.714
We're doctor. Right. Right.

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:49.482
Our goal is to take care of our clients.

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:50.383
Sure. Sure.

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:51.117
And for today,

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:53.286
we're going to be just looking.

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:55.922
And, you know, the judge in Texas

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:59.325
in his ruling said that the FDA.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:00.360
27 years ago

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:03.062
improperly or improperly approved

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.497
this abortion pill.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:05.465
And that you know,

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:06.699
he had taken into account

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:08.668
or the FDA has not taken into account

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.103
the physiological effects

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:13.139
that taking this drug has on women.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:14.540
What do you say to that?

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:19.412
The physiological effects of misoprostol

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.313
and misoprostol,

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:21.347
the two medications

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:23.549
that go into this medication, abortion,

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:24.250
are essentially

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.352
the same as the physiological effects

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:27.787
of a miscarriage.

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:29.589
So many,

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:31.324
many women have had miscarriages.

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:33.393
It is not a pleasant experience,

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:36.062
but it is not inherently unsafe.

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:38.064
The judge also alleged

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.632
that there were psychological effects

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:41.000
from these medications.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.802
Let me be very clear.

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.171
There are more than 50 years of studies

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:45.872
showing that

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.974
the psychological effects of abortion

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.208
are nil.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.009
What effects

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:52.545
women's mental health is being forced

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:54.781
to carry a pregnancy to term?

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:56.816
The availability of safe

00:06:56.816 --> 00:07:00.420
and legal abortion is a strong protection

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.689
to women's mental health And lastly,

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:04.991
because as I read,

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:06.793
mifepristone is typically

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:07.827
used in combination

00:07:07.827 --> 00:07:08.461
with another drug

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.563
that you just mentioned, misoprostol,

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.498
that is still available on the market

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:14.400
so do you think the alternative could be

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.068
just using misoprostol

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:16.969
for those

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:19.272
who need a medication, abortion?

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:20.673
And let's say, you know,

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:21.774
this pause continues

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:25.244
or should this continue?

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:25.611
Yes.

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:26.546
Using misoprostol

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:28.614
alone is certainly an option,

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:30.483
but it is less effective

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:31.217
and associated

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:33.019
with a higher number of side effects.

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:35.188
The combination of the two medications,

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:36.522
the reason we give them together

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.591
is because they work and they're safe.

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:39.992
So it would be a shame

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.594
for the women of America

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:42.995
if they have to resort to

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:45.264
a single medication regimen

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:46.833
that is less effective

00:07:46.833 --> 00:07:48.734
than what they currently have access to.

